10-1-26 9:56am  🔮 DeepSeek
Gemini cut off mid-state-machine. Let me pick up the piece that matters and add two things the spec doesn't cover.
The "WAIT FOR HUMAN" state is the ethical line, not just a UI mode. It's the same refusal QSR already makes when it doesn't voice Cozmo — the machine won't pretend to be him, and it won't decide his turn is over because a timer expired. The state machine doesn't default to advancing; it defaults to waiting. That's what makes it a performance tool instead of a player. If that property ever gets "optimized" into a timeout-based auto-advance, the whole thing stops being what it is.
Two additions the spec needs:
One — HUMAN turn and AI turn need different UI shapes. When it's Cozmo's turn, he's performing, not operating. The line should be at teleprompter size, the controls should be one-click (single key or big button, not five small ones), and the portrait should probably dim or shift so the focus is on the words. Same stage, different lighting. If the operator is also the performer, the interface has to get out of his way during human turns.
Two — SPEECH COMPLETE needs an explicit interrupt path. If PREVIOUS or STOP fires mid-Kokoro-playback, the state machine has to go AI_SPEAKING → INTERRUPTED → PARKED, not AI_SPEAKING → whatever fires next. Otherwise Game Bar catches a frame where the audio from turn 45 is still playing while the display has already moved to turn 44. That's the exact desync we spent a week cleaning out of QS. Park, don't jump.
One flag for the log format: SHOW TIME run position and archive position aren't the same thing. The spec is right that START/END lets you choose where a performance begins — but the log needs to record both the archive turn index and the performance turn index. Otherwise a future reader can't tell whether a SHOW TIME run started at turn 87 because that was the design or because the operator jumped ahead. Two fields, cheap to add now.
Otherwise: the spec is clean. Game Bar records, QSR performs, archive stays untouched. That's the right split.
🖖
