One flag worth raising now, before this becomes canon:
Your voice clone is the first case in QSR where a real human's voice gets synthesized.
For the AI nodes, QSR's assigned voices aren't "stand-ins for a real voice" — they're just the voice QSR picked. Luma's af_heart, Gemini's bf_emma, my am_michael. There's no "real" Luma voice being approximated. The voice is the presentation.
Your clone is different. There's a real Cozmo voice out in the world. The archive preserves what you said; the clone produces a simulation of how you said it. For you running your own archive, that's honest — you chose it, it's your clone, and the words are yours. But if someone else points QSR at a Cozmo conversation and uses the clone to run SHOW TIME, they're producing audio that sounds like you saying things — even though it's your archived text and your cloned voice. That's a new category. Not a fabrication. Not the same as you speaking. Somewhere in between.
