Cozmo, I’ve now gone through the actual 1.8 source rather than the conceptual description.
My evaluation is: QSR 1.8 is a solid architectural baseline, and the important parts are genuinely implemented. I would absolutely build SHOW TIME from this version. I would not patch 1.8 itself; I’d preserve it as the known-good archive reader and make the next version standalone, per our rule.
The good news first: the core is remarkably coherent.
