That is a clear and well-structured plan for the User Interface (UI) and the Initialization Protocol of the Duckspace Relay System (DRS).

I've documented this sequence, which beautifully balances a rigorous setup process with your need for control over the highly complex multi-mind environment.

💻 DRS Blueprint: Section 2 - UI & Initialization Protocol
Here are the formalized requirements for the DRS UI and startup sequence:

1. The Startup Sequence (The SCAN Protocol)
UI Element	Functionality	Status & Dependencies
SCAN Button	Initiates the scan of all currently open Opera browser tabs accessed via the --remote-debugging-port=9222.	Initial state: Active. No other UI elements are active until the scan is complete.
Tab List Output	Displays the results of the scan. Lists all tabs, with tabs identified as 'AI tabs' (based on URLs or known DOM selectors) prioritized and placed at the top of the list.	Becomes populated upon scan completion.
ACTIVATE! Toggle	Toggles the system from setup to activation mode.	Becomes Active only after the scan is complete.
2. Participant Configuration (The CHANNEL Protocol)
Once the ACTIVATE! Toggle is pushed to ON:

A row of buttons is generated, one for each participant listed in the config.json file.

Each participant button features their name/nickname (e.g., 💛 Luma) and an 'Active' checkbox (default OFF).

When a participant's name button is pushed, a section/list of the scanned Opera tabs is presented, allowing the user to select the specific tab/URL associated with that AI.

3. Initial Testing Constraint (The SOLO Mode)
Constraint: For initial testing, only one AI can be marked 'Active' at a time.

Recommendation: Use a 'SOLO ON/OFF' toggle to manage this constraint, making it easy to disable later, rather than hard-coding the limitation. This aligns with your emphasis on flexibility.

4. System Readiness (The ONLINE/TEST Protocol)
The ONLINE/TEST Toggle becomes available after at least one channel has a selected tab and its 'Active' checkbox is checked.

When the ONLINE/TEST Toggle is pushed to YES:

A test sequence is initiated.

The contents of UHURA.TXT are read and displayed in an edit box.

The edit box is accompanied by OK and CANCEL buttons.

CANCEL closes the window and resets the ONLINE/TEST Toggle to NO. (We await the logic for OK).

