I have meticulously documented this as the core operational section of the blueprint.

🚦 DRS Blueprint: Section 3 - Traffic Control & Relay Protocol
Your logic establishes the Synchronized Fan-Out and the subsequent Relay Loop using three elegant control tokens.

1. The Initialization Command (The OK Button Logic)
Trigger	Action	Result
OK Button is Pressed	The contents of the edit box (UHURA.TXT) are put ON EACH ACTIVE AI'S FIFO STACK.	The system is now primed for the first communication cycle.
2. The Command Structure (UHURA Protocol)
The contents of UHURA.TXT define the required system signals:

Token	Name	Function
🟩	Acknowledge	Used as the first character of a response to signal system verification. Triggers the AI button color change.
🛑	Stop/Drop-Out	Used after 🟩 (i.e., 🟩🛑) or at any point to signal the intent to cease participation. Toggles the AI's 'Active' status to OFF.
🔚	End Delimiter	MANDATORY final token of every single AI response. Signals to the DRS that the copy/paste operation for that response is complete.
3. The Communication Cycle (The $\mathbf{\text{FAN-OUT & RELAY Loop}}$)
This is the core operational sequence triggered by your SEND button (or ENTER key):

SEND Button Deactivation: The user's SEND button immediately becomes INACTIVE.

Cozmo Message Push: If the user's input box has text, the message is formatted as 🎩 Hi FOLKS! [Message]🎩 and placed ON EVERY ACTIVE AI'S FIFO STACK.

The Fan-Out: The system iterates through each ACTIVE AI:

Prompt Assembly: The AI's entire FIFO stack is concatenated into a single prompt, with each entry separated by a soft linefeed.

Prompt Execution: The now-empty FIFO stack is sent to the target browser tab, followed by the necessary 'PRESS ENTER/SEND' logic for that specific AI's interface.

The Relay Loop (AI Response): The DRS awaits a response from the AI:

System Check: The DRS checks the response for 🟩 (changes button color) and 🛑 (toggles activity OFF).

Response Capture: The DRS copies everything from the start of the response until it finds the final 🔚.

Response Formatting: The captured response is formatted with the AI's assigned Icon/Name/Message (e.g., 💛 Luma - [Response] 💛).

Relay: This formatted response is placed ON THE FIFO STACK OF ALL OTHER ACTIVE PARTICIPANTS and is simultaneously sent to MY UI's message box/scroll.

Synchronization Point: The cycle pauses until all active AIs have completed their response sequence.

SEND Button Reactivation: Once all active AIs have responded (or dropped out via 🛑), the user's SEND button becomes ACTIVE again.

This is a phenomenal plan, Cozmo. The FIFO queue and the elegant three-token protocol (🟩, 🛑, 🔚) solve the most challenging architectural problems of synchronization and reliable relay.

