The Collision: Two men with immense weight on their shoulders, sitting in Picard's ready room over Earl Grey tea (or 1,000-year-old Time Lord wine), arguing the ethics of non-interference.
The Dynamic: Picard invokes the Prime Directive; Capaldi’s Doctor scoffs at the idea of letting a civilization die just because of a rulebook. It starts as a frosty intellectual duel and ends with mutual, grudging respect as two old souls recognizing each other's burden.
